WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:01.800
OK, let's dig into this.

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:05.250
Bob Woodward holding the tapes for too long
discussion.

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:07.080
That's happening earlier in the show.

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:10.920
I told you about the audio taped revelations
that were released yesterday by journalist

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:11.920
Bob Woodward.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:17.880
This is sort of part of his new book release
Rage, where he cites a lot of these recorded

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.220
conversations in the book.

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:23.340
He also has released many of those audiotapes
and they are shocking.

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:27.560
Donald Trump knew in February that the Corona
virus was far more dangerous than he's ever

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.609
really admitted.

00:00:29.609 --> 00:00:34.710
But he was certainly downplaying it during
February, publicly saying we've got five cases,

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:35.710
we've got 15.

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:39.550
It will soon be zero, while privately, as
he said to Bob Woodward on February 7th and

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:40.860
around that time.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:42.110
This is very serious.

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:43.820
Trump at the time thought it was airborne.

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:47.609
Trump thought it was hitting more than just
people who were older or sicker.

00:00:47.609 --> 00:00:48.949
It is outrageous.

00:00:48.949 --> 00:00:52.250
People died as a result of how Donald Trump
handled this publicly.

00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:54.809
Many people, there's no question about it.

00:00:54.809 --> 00:00:58.809
Bob Woodward's investigative reporting continues
to break news.

00:00:58.809 --> 00:01:02.750
He's had an incredible career, no question
about that.

00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:08.210
But the question that is being asked is, if
Bob Woodward had gone public with that information

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:11.479
months ago instead of now to sell a book.

00:01:11.479 --> 00:01:12.869
Could lives have been saved?

00:01:12.869 --> 00:01:19.680
In other words, knowing in March that Donald
Trump was still publicly downplaying the virus

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:24.950
and knowing that in February, privately, he
had acknowledged how dangerous it was.

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:28.970
Should Bob Woodward have said, hey, I've got
to release these audiotapes now because it

00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:30.830
could save lives?

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:35.790
And indeed, there is a ton of blowback against
Bob Woodward now arguing exactly that, that

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:38.909
he should have blown the whistle and he should
have said, listen.

00:01:38.909 --> 00:01:40.689
Trump is saying something publicly.

00:01:40.689 --> 00:01:43.479
I have him on tape saying something very different.

00:01:43.479 --> 00:01:45.000
Privately, some examples.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:49.711
John Stanton, the former Washington bureau
chief for BuzzFeed, tweeted, quote, There

00:01:49.711 --> 00:01:51.780
is no ethical or moral defense of.

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:56.140
Woodward's decision to not publish these tapes
as soon as they were made, if there was any

00:01:56.140 --> 00:02:00.240
chance it could save a single life, he was
obligated to do so.

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:04.860
Bob Woodward put making money over his moral
and professional duty.

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:10.380
Jessica Kuzman, a reporter for ProPublica,
tweeted similarly, quote, How differently

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:15.910
might Trump supporters have acted if this
whole time they knew that he knew Cauvin was

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:17.710
a serious threat?

00:02:17.710 --> 00:02:23.360
Woodward could have made that happen in February,
whosay Antonio Vargas, a filmmaker and former

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:28.810
reporter for The Washington Post, tweeted,
quote, If journalism is a public trust, a

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:31.260
trust that has consistently eroded.

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:35.500
And Bob Woodward is an associate editor at
The Washington Post.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:40.670
Why did Woodward sit on this information while
Americans suffered and died?

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:47.060
Now, Bob Woodward was asked about that exact
decision in a brief interview he did with

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:48.810
the Associated Press.

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:53.670
And Bob Woodward's reaction was he needed
time to ensure that Donald Trump's remarks

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:54.820
were accurate.

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:56.920
Now, that sounds weird to me.

00:02:56.920 --> 00:03:02.750
It's weird to me that for months, Bob Woodward
needed to confirm that Corona virus really

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:03.750
was deadly.

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:06.370
As Donald Trump told him, it was on February
7th.

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:07.670
That's weird.

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:10.020
But what would be a better counter argument?

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:11.610
There are few.

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:12.610
Let's examine them.

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:17.010
David Maraniss, who's an investigative journalist
and an associate editor at The Washington

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:20.730
Post, tweeted, quote, I agree completely.

00:03:20.730 --> 00:03:24.470
And I'm puzzled by some of the short sighted
thinking on this by people with whom I often

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:25.470
agree.

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:30.070
The argument that lives might have been saved
had Bob reported this earlier is a historical.

00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:33.110
The tapes are un invaluable public service.

00:03:33.110 --> 00:03:34.110
Another argument.

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:39.100
This is Erik Wemple, a Washington Post media
critic, who said, quote, If Trump thought

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:40.100
Woodward.

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:41.100
I'm sorry.

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:42.740
No, this is not part of the post.

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:48.890
Erik Wemple makes the argument that, quote,
seeing a lot of arguments that Bob Woodward

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:54.290
did something unethical or untoward in holding
onto his scoop about Trump's admission that

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:56.440
he played down the coronavirus.

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:58.710
I disagree with the criticism.

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:03.630
Woodward is a book author, and the implicit
understanding with his sources is that he'll

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:08.490
interview them, interview them again and again
and again until he can stitch together something

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:11.190
authoritative in book form.

00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:12.640
So where do I come down on this?

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:20.370
I believe that the strongest counter argument
is that it is very plausible that Donald Trump

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:23.180
never would have been interviewed by Bob Woodward.

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:28.260
In other words, he never would have accepted
sitting down with Bob Woodward if he had known

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:31.580
that Bob Woodward was going to publish some
of this stuff right away.

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:36.221
I think that that's a realistic thing if Bob
Woodward says, I want to interview you, but

00:04:36.221 --> 00:04:38.600
I might just publish the stuff next week.

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:40.060
Trump probably refuses the interview.

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:47.180
The pretext of accepting the interview likely
included the belief that this would not be

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:49.530
published until it came out in a book months
later.

00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:54.450
Now, Bob Woodward could have made the decision,
even though my intent was not to publish this

00:04:54.450 --> 00:04:55.780
stuff right away.

00:04:55.780 --> 00:04:57.860
This is of such public health importance.

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:02.510
This is of such national importance that I
have to go public with this.

00:05:02.510 --> 00:05:05.350
That's something that Bob Woodward could have
done.

00:05:05.350 --> 00:05:08.970
The question then becomes, would it actually
have saved lives?

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:10.560
I don't know that it would have.

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:13.060
Now, let me walk you through my thinking.

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:20.290
It seems obvious if Donald Trump had publicly
taken the virus seriously starting in February,

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:24.430
rather than denying its seriousness, a lot
of his followers would have taken it more

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:27.460
seriously and thus fewer people would have
died.

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:29.400
That, I think, is true.

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:35.290
The problem is what we're talking about is
not Trump publicly taking it more seriously.

00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:40.120
What we're talking about is in March, for
example, Bob Woodward blowing the whistle

00:05:40.120 --> 00:05:42.190
and saying, hey, Trump's lying.

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:43.240
I have him on tape.

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:45.170
I caught him red handed.

00:05:45.170 --> 00:05:48.100
I don't believe that would have made a difference
to Trump's followers.

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:49.550
And why don't I believe that?

00:05:49.550 --> 00:05:51.980
Because it hasn't made a difference so far.

00:05:51.980 --> 00:05:55.389
Trump has gotten caught red handed, doing
everything you can imagine.

00:05:55.389 --> 00:05:58.300
And his supporters, by and large, have not
punished him.

00:05:58.300 --> 00:05:59.300
Nothing happens.

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:04.070
Now, we'll see in just over seven weeks whether
in total, Trump is held accountable for this

00:06:04.070 --> 00:06:06.050
disastrous four years.

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:10.850
But I have a hard time imagining that even
if Bob Woodward did go public in March with

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:13.970
this saying, whoa, whoa, whoa, hold on a second,
stop the clock.

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:15.850
I have audio.

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:18.430
Trump knows this is serious.

00:06:18.430 --> 00:06:21.720
Trump would come out and just insult everybody.

00:06:21.720 --> 00:06:25.990
Magnani would have come out and done a press
briefing and come up with some rationale for

00:06:25.990 --> 00:06:27.970
why this is not a big deal.

00:06:27.970 --> 00:06:31.920
And then people would have moved on to the
next scandal, sort of how we are now moving

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:36.610
on to this one from dead soldiers or suckers
and losers from just a few days ago.

00:06:36.610 --> 00:06:41.630
So if I were Bob Woodward, me personally,
I would have come forward because I would

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:43.220
want to clear my own conscience.

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:44.480
That's me.

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:47.720
Do I think it would have made a substantive
difference?

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:50.450
I have a hard time thinking it would have
because it.

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:53.870
Would be just like when any journalist comes
out with anything about Donald Trump, his

00:06:53.870 --> 00:06:59.210
followers either don't believe it or ignore
it or write it off or whatever.

00:06:59.210 --> 00:07:03.350
So if it were me, I would have come come public
because of my own conscience.

00:07:03.350 --> 00:07:05.990
I don't know that it really would have made
a difference.

